{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 192.0.2.77 attempted a path traversal attack using various encoding techniques (standard dot-dot-slash, URL encoding, and double encoding) to access sensitive system files such as /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow, and Windows win.ini. The resulting HTTP status codes (400 and 403) indicate that the web server or application successfully blocked the unauthorized requests, preventing file disclosure.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement strict input validation and allowlisting for all file retrieval parameters to ensure only expected filenames or IDs are processed.",
    "Use built-in framework functions or APIs designed to safely resolve file paths (such as java.nio.file.Path.normalize() or realpath() in PHP) and verify that the target file remains within the intended root directory.",
    "Block the malicious source IP 192.0.2.77 at the web application firewall (WAF) or perimeter firewall level and monitor for continued scanning behavior."
  ]
}
